# The Claude Code half of the daily skill record: the native /skill-doctor capture (lifetime uses per skill) and the child-usage.mjs --lanes-sweep Skill calls. The Codex half is skill-invoke-rate-codex.service;
# each has its own timeouts and its own record, so a slow Codex scan never leaves this half unmeasured (docs/decisions/2026-10-12-skill-invoke-rate-timer.md).
# Render @REPOSITORY@ to the live clone, %h/code/native-agent-stack-live, matching stack-currency.service: a detached worktree of origin/main, which
# daily_skill_usage.py accepts (any commit of origin/main; it refuses a feature branch and commits of the clone's own, and so does --render-units).
# Render @PYTHON@ and @NODE@ to installed interpreter paths:
#   python3 tools/skill-usage/daily_skill_usage.py --render-units <dir> --repository %h/code/native-agent-stack-live --python <python> --node <node>
# The CC installs this file after landing; the authoring lane runs fixture tests only. TimeoutStartSec exceeds the sum of the half's command limits
# (daily_skill_usage.py half_budget; a test pins it): the capture 300 s + 60 s, the sweep 600 s, and a minute of margin.
[Unit]
Description=Daily native skill invocation report, Claude Code half

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=@REPOSITORY@
UMask=0077
Nice=10
# Writes: the record directory below and nothing else that the directives make read-only (the half's own record, the combined record the Fleet page reads, and the lock that serialises the combined refresh; both halves write the same directory).
# ProtectSystem=strict mounts the whole file hierarchy read-only, ProtectHome=read-only does the same for the home directory (the live clone and the client's own state included), and ReadWritePaths= opens the one
# directory that is written (systemd.exec(5), systemd 259.5). PrivateTmp=true gives the client its own /tmp under ProtectSystem=strict; /dev, /proc and /sys keep rules of their own (man/systemd.exec.xml L1381-L1384).
# These need a mount namespace, and a manager that cannot create one starts the unit without these directives and says nothing, unless the unit also asks for something it cannot run without (systemd/systemd-stable@387a14a7b67b,
# v255.4: src/core/exec-invoke.c L3212-L3237 and src/core/namespace.c L2488-L2497; the manual calls them "gracefully turned off", man/systemd.exec.xml L1359-L1364; the GitHub-hosted runner's manager does exactly that,
# docs/decisions/2026-10-12-skill-invoke-rate-timer.md, review round 5). TemporaryFileSystem=/srv:ro is that ask: insist_on_sandboxing() (exec-invoke.c L2849-L2888, called at L3217-L3233) is true for it, so a manager that
# cannot make the mount namespace stops the unit with status 226/NAMESPACE (exec_invoke, exec-invoke.c L4655-L4664; man/systemd.exec.xml L4356-L4358) instead of running it unconfined. It exists only for that: it hides /srv,
# which nothing in this unit reads (the clone, the interpreters and the records are under the home, and rendering refuses a path under /srv). PrivateUsers=true asks for the user namespace in the same way (status 217/USER,
# exec_invoke, L4595-L4609; man L4316-L4317), and in a user service the file system directives work in conjunction with it (man L1366-L1370). So the unit runs in the mount namespace these directives describe or it does not
# start (226 or 217). That is no boundary for what is started outside systemd, against a later change of the host's mounts by a privileged process, or on a platform without systemd, and a mount the unit asks for itself (an
# explicit bind) is exempt from the recursion. The directory must exist before the unit starts (mkdir -m 0700 -p): ReadWritePaths= without a leading "-" fails closed on a missing path. PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 reaches every
# interpreter the service starts (-B on the parent alone would not).
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=read-only
ReadWritePaths=%h/.local/state/native-agent-stack/coordination/command-center/skills
PrivateTmp=true
PrivateUsers=true
TemporaryFileSystem=/srv:ro
Environment=PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
Environment=PATH=%h/.local/bin:%h/.local/share/mise/shims:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
TimeoutStartSec=17min
ExecStart="@PYTHON@" "@REPOSITORY@/tools/skill-usage/daily_skill_usage.py" --half claude --node "@NODE@" --claude-root %h/.claude/projects --window 7 --out %h/.local/state/native-agent-stack/coordination/command-center/skills/skill-invoke-rate-claude-latest.json --combined-out %h/.local/state/native-agent-stack/coordination/command-center/skills/skill-invoke-rate-latest.json --other-record %h/.local/state/native-agent-stack/coordination/command-center/skills/skill-invoke-rate-codex-latest.json
